The value supplied to switch is matched with the appropriate case.

Answer: A case represents a value that can be matched with the value supplied to switch. Example:

```java
switch (number) {
case 1:
System.out.println("Sunday");
break;
}
```

If number is 1, the statement belonging to case 1 executes.

Answer: If a matching case is found and there is no break, execution continues into the cases below it. This continued execution is the behavior demonstrated when break statements were omitted. Example:

```java
switch (number) {
case 1:
System.out.println("Sunday");
case 2:
System.out.println("Monday");
case 3:
System.out.println("Tuesday");
}
```

Sample Input: 1 Output: Sunday Monday Tuesday

